I'm assuming this is all related to Keylime's installer.sh script. Keylime =
should support newer tools (looks like 4.2):
https://github.com/keylime/keylime/blob/149dffe7aa7ba8296689710854317545778=
d2414/keylime/tpm/tpm_main.py#L263

I would modify their install to set newer versions of the tools and tss:
diff --git a/installer.sh b/installer.sh
index 64a0b9ca9143..5ee4782df833 100755
--- a/installer.sh
+++ b/installer.sh
@@ -14,8 +14,8 @@ TPM2SIM_SRC=3Dhttp://sourceforge.net/projects/ibmswtpm2/f=
iles/ibmtpm1119.tar.gz/do
 KEYLIME_VER=3D"master"
 TPM4720_VER=3D"master"
 GOLANG_VER=3D"1.13.1"
-TPM2TSS_VER=3D"2.0.x"
-TPM2TOOLS_VER=3D"3.X"
+TPM2TSS_VER=3D"3.0.3"
+TPM2TOOLS_VER=3D"4.2"

 # Minimum version requirements
 MIN_PYTHON_VERSION=3D"3.6.7"

